scripts/__pycache__/
__pycache__/
qa-report.txt
# the fix loop's scratch class (issue #390): the loop used to write `qa-report.txt.notes`
# beside the report, and a bot's `git add -A` committed the 0-byte file into PR #387.
# The loop now keeps its notes outside the checkout; this covers any other sibling.
qa-report.txt.*
comment.md
# issue-bot working files: the issue text it implements and the PR body it opens
# (AGENTS.md: every implementation run analyses what it touched and files what it
# found). The analysis itself is NOT scratch since issue #1493 — it is the tracked,
# per-issue `findings/<issue>.md` the shape-aware `make findings-check-for-pr` gate
# in qa-validate reads.
# (issue #1493) The pre-#1493 shared append point: ONE root `findings.md` that every
# implementation run appended a `## <title>` section to, so any two open PRs answered
# `CONFLICT (content): Merge conflict in findings.md` and GitHub's auto-merge refused
# them both (measured on PR #1488). The historical sections moved to
# `findings/history.md`; a stray root write is scratch and must never reach a commit,
# so the path is ignored here but stays OFF scripts/issue_bot_working_files.txt
# because nothing writes it anymore.
findings.md
issue.md
pr-body.md
# issue-bot's start comment (the window the reviewer defers to) and the reviewer's
# working files: the rewritten body, its one comment, and the live body it compares
# itself against. All of them are written on the runner, never committed.
start.md
issue-body.md
comment-window.md
current-body.md
reply.md
triage.md
# the captured agent stream and its REDACTED copy (issue #351): the raw capture is
# never printed and never uploaded — only `make scrub-log`'s redacted output is —
# and neither may a stray `git add -A` commit.
implement.log
implement.scrubbed.log
review.log
review.scrubbed.log
# the captured agent stream of a PUBLIC target that runs the agent (`make search-*`,
# `make fix` — the `scrubbed_run` seam, issue #355) and its REDACTED copy. Only the
# redacted one is ever printed or uploaded.
hermes-run.log
hermes-run.scrubbed.log
# the gitleaks JSON report `make secret-scan` writes into the mounted tree, read
# by scripts/secret_scan_report.py and deleted in the same recipe (issue #836);
# per-run unique names, because recreating a path the host just deleted hits a
# stale virtiofs dentry and FTLs gitleaks — a fixed name is a flaky gate.
.secret-scan-report*.json
# the throwaway tree of make secret-scan-self-test, repo-local because macOS's
# /var/folders TMPDIR cannot be mounted into a colima container — gitleaks would
# scan 0 bytes there (issue #836).
.secret-self-test-tmp/
